    "body": "> Can't the prescan also parse with scripting disabled mode in those cases?\r\n\r\nThat seems implementation-wise very reasonable even if theoretically less so. (Why would scripting state potentially change the encoding?) Mostly I didn't want to say anything too definite without testing how XHR behaves in Blink and WebKit.\r\n\r\n> (I wonder if we should eliminate the scripting enabled/disabled parse modes and always parse as scripting enabled.)\r\n\r\nThat seems out of scope for this issue but could have benefits in terms of reducing gotchas in markup sanitizer scripts.",
