    "body": "http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/9562 -- XHR with meta charset in noscript.\r\nChrome Canary: windows-1253. Safari TP: UTF-8. Firefox Nightly: windows-1253.\r\n\r\nhttp://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/9563 -- XHR with meta charset in head.\r\nChrome Canary: windows-1253. Safari TP: UTF-8. Firefox Nightly: windows-1253.\r\n\r\nhttp://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/9564 -- XHR with meta charset in xmp.\r\nChrome Canary: UTF-8. Safari TP: UTF-8. Firefox Nightly: windows-1253.\r\n\r\nSo Chrome Canary tokenizes as-if scripting is disabled for XHR. Safari TP always uses UTF-8 (but I only checked `data:` URLs).",
