    "body": "So if I'm reading this correctly, the effective change here is to ignore `<meta charset>` inside `<noscript>` always (including XHR?). Is that right? It appears (from this [test page](https://hsivonen.com/test/moz/meta/in-noscript.htm)) that all three engines currently **do** process those `<meta>` tags, at least in normal browsing. Do you have a sense for compat here? It seems like a very corner case to put `<meta>` inside `<noscript>` but you never know.",
