    "created_at": "2021-09-16T18:38:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-16T18:38:25Z",
    "body": "> I'm confused why any of the changes proposed here or that you're implementing in Firefox would have any impact on authoring conformance requirements, i.e. what we consider best practice and want to promote for authors.\r\n\r\nIf we accept this spec change, the requirement to having the encoding meta within the first 1024 bytes isn't that important for any UA that implements the spec change. The better advice would be \"the earlier, the better\", but 1024 would no longer be an important cliff as long as the requirement to have it as a child of `head` is complied with.\r\n\r\nWe could choose to retain the 1024-byte advice for the benefit of UAs that implement what the spec says now.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
