    "body": "I'm OK with requiring the encoding declaration to be the first child of `head`. Especially if we will remove the 1024 byte check, checking that it is as present early as possible seems good.\r\n\r\nI don't see much value in keeping the 1024 byte and the no-charrefs requirements temporarily, if we know we want to remove them. Change all the document conformance requirements at the same time, to reduce churn, imo.",
