    "updated_at": "2021-09-21T07:38:35Z",
    "body": "Pages in httparchive (dataset of ~7.4 million pages) that use an encoding declaration in `noscript`:\r\n\r\nNone.\r\n\r\nActually, [I found 5 pages](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1yMfK6UycgnBwiVr9qnfnY5IhMYxwJXHazHaQ4EQCz1U/edit?usp=sharing), but they are all false positives. They seem to be either\r\n\r\n* using `noscript` only to WebPageTest (which is [used by httparchive to collect data](https://httparchive.org/faq#how-is-the-data-gathered)), to \"cheat\" and get better performance score. or\r\n* include a whole HTML document in `noscript` elements. There's an encoding declaration in the head (not in noscript), so the later one would have no effect anyway.\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Query</summary>\r\n\r\n```sql\r\nSELECT\r\n  *\r\nFROM (\r\n  SELECT\r\n    page,\r\n    url,\r\n    ARRAY_TO_STRING(REGEXP_EXTRACT_ALL(body, r'(?i)(<noscript(?:\\s+[^>]+)?>(?:[^<]|<[^\\/]|<\\/[^n]|<\\/n[^o]|<\\/no[^s]|<\\/nos[^c]).*?<\\/noscript>)'), '\\n') AS markup\r\n  FROM\r\n    `httparchive.response_bodies.2021_08_01_mobile` )\r\nWHERE\r\n  markup != \"\" AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(markup, r'(?i)(<meta\\s+(?:charset\\s*=|http-equiv\\s*=\\s*[\"\\']?content-type[\"\\']?\\s+content\\s*=\\s*[\"\\']?text\\/html\\s*;\\s*charset=|content\\s*=\\s*[\"\\']?text\\/html\\s*;\\s*charset=[a-z0-9_-]+[\"\\']?\\s+http-equiv\\s*=\\s*[\"\\']?content-type[\"\\']?))')\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
