    "updated_at": "2021-09-29T13:59:41Z",
    "body": "I found another case (in addition to `noscript`, that is) where WebKit and Blink differ from what I'm proposing:\r\n\r\nSince they don't implement real foreign content rules for their prescan, the result differs if the [`meta` is in a CDATA section in SVG and there is a `>` before the `meta` within the CDATA section](https://hsivonen.com/test/moz/meta/in-svg-in-cdata-after-gt.htm), so that the `>` ends the bogus comment when the CDATA section tokenizes as a bogus comment.\r\n\r\nI think it's even less worthwhile to emulate this behavior than the `noscript` behavior.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/930147678/reactions",
